# .dockerignore — build-context exclusions for the api-server / macro-project image
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (Fable Plan 2, cluster C0.1 / finding M15):
# The image is built from environment.yml (Dockerfile step 4) and then bakes the
# repo via `COPY . .` (step 6).  At runtime the compose services bind-mount the
# live repo at /app (`.:/app`), so the *baked* copy is overridden anyway — only
# the conda env layer needs to be correct.  A clean `docker compose build
# api-server` was failing at `COPY . .` because the build context contained a
# file the host filesystem could not read (`docs/other/'pop_up_representative'.png`,
# single-quotes literally in the name, raising `input/output error` on copy).
# Excluding it — plus the heavy, non-runtime, churn-prone paths below — makes the
# image build reproducibly and keeps the context small/fast.  None of these paths
# are needed inside the image (the live bind-mount provides everything at runtime).

# --- the unreadable asset that broke `COPY . .` (host I/O error) ---
docs/other/

# --- VCS / tooling metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# --- nested git worktrees (created by the agent harness; not part of the image) ---
.claude/worktrees/

# --- Python / test caches and build artifacts ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- local env / secrets (provided at runtime via env_file / bind-mount) ---
.env
.venv/
venv/

# --- knowledge-graph + scratch output (not runtime deps) ---
graphify-out/
tmp/

# --- editor / OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
